# Animation Approval

- Do not create, edit, replace, restyle, retune, or remove animations without first describing the intended change and waiting for explicit user approval.
- This includes GSAP timelines, ScrollTrigger, CSS keyframes, transitions, transforms used for motion, and choreography of existing sequences.
- Treat current animations as correct unless the user says they are not. Do not "improve" motion while working on unrelated tasks.
- If a request could affect motion, ask first. Do not implement a motion alternative "just in case."

# GSAP Animation Standards

- Inspect installed GSAP and framework integration versions before using APIs. Do not assume a plugin is installed.
- Prefer @gsap/react and useGSAP() in React projects when compatible with the existing setup.
- Register GSAP plugins correctly and only once where appropriate.
- Scope selectors to component roots. Avoid global selectors that can animate unrelated elements.
- Ensure timelines, event listeners, ScrollTriggers, and other resources are cleaned up correctly on unmount and re-render.
- Make animations safe under React Strict Mode and avoid duplicate timelines or ScrollTriggers.
- Prefer transform and opacity for smooth animation. Avoid repeatedly animating layout-triggering properties when possible.
- Use ScrollTrigger deliberately. Avoid excessive pinned sections, competing scroll effects, and unnecessary scrub animations.
- Coordinate animation timing, easing, stagger, and transitions into a coherent motion system.
- Avoid animating every element. Motion must support hierarchy, storytelling, or usability.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion and provide meaningful non-animated behavior.
- Keep interactions responsive on touch devices and avoid hover-only essential functionality.
- For video backgrounds, consider autoplay restrictions, muted playback, playsInline, poster frames, loading strategy, and mobile data usage.
- Test scrolling, resizing, route changes, and component remounting when applicable.
- Do not claim an animation works until it has been verified in the browser when browser access is available.